<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_BEN_DEPEND_RECON_DM — BIP reconciliation report contract v1 for
    BenDependent (Benefit dependents / person contacts, loaded via HCM Data
    Loader). Design doc: "BIP reconciliation report contract - v1" (nine
    columns, six parameters, keyset pagination) plus its HDL note: "each HDL
    object gets a Contract v1 report whose rows are the BASE tier (key + Fusion
    id); its ERROR rows are optional because HDL failures arrive per-record in
    the HDL response and are tagged [FUSION_ERROR] before the report runs."

    BASE-TIER ONLY. An HDL load has no interface table, so this report returns
    the BASE tier: one row per migrated dependent that Fusion positively
    confirmed by writing a HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP entry, with the Fusion base
    id as FUSION_ID. This is the same base-tier proof the Salaries reconciler
    uses, and the design doc endorses it for HDL objects.

    HOW THIS OBJECT ACTUALLY LOADS (verified live 2026-09-20, fin_impl /
    ApplicationDB_FSCM):
      * DMT_BEN_DEPEND_HDL_GEN_PKG writes a PersonBenefitBalance.dat whose
        business object / discriminator is 'PersonBenefitBalance' (the more
        specific DependentBenefitBalance is NOT a valid HDL discriminator — the
        three benefit sub-objects all share PersonBenefitBalance, see that
        package and objects/Benefits/README.md), whose SourceSystemId is
        (prefixed PERSON_NUMBER) || '_BENDEP', and whose SourceSystemOwner is
        'HRC_SQLLOADER'. That same value is the BenDependent TFM row's RECON_KEY
        (DMT_BEN_DEPEND_TRANSFORM_PKG).
      * On load, Fusion records one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per record:
        OBJECT_NAME = 'PersonBenefitBalance',
        SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER = 'HRC_SQLLOADER',
        SOURCE_SYSTEM_ID = our _BENDEP key,
        SURROGATE_ID = the Fusion-assigned benefit-balance base id
        (BEN_PER_BNFTS_BAL_F.PER_BNFTS_BAL_ID).

    BASE TABLE / FUSION_ID. On this pod BEN_PER_BNFTS_BAL_F is selectable by the
    BIP reporting user and its PER_BNFTS_BAL_ID joins the PersonBenefitBalance
    SURROGATE_IDs one-for-one (verified 2026-09-20: all 10 HRC_SQLLOADER-owned
    PersonBenefitBalance key-map rows join back to a real PER_BNFTS_BAL_ID). The
    query therefore JOINS the base table and returns b.per_bnfts_bal_id as
    FUSION_ID, so every FUSION_ID is guaranteed a real base-table primary key —
    the strongest base-tier proof (same shape as the Salaries / older
    BenDependent reports). The HRC_SQLLOADER owner filter guarantees Fusion-
    seeded PersonBenefitBalance rows (owner FUSION, 828 of them on the pod) are
    never counted.

    OUR OWN ROWS ARE NOT YET PRESENT. No _BENDEP key exists on the demo pod
    (verified 2026-09-20: zero HRC_SQLLOADER PersonBenefitBalance rows match
    '%\_BENDEP'). Employee benefit enrollment is not configured on the demo
    instance and the migrated test workers are not enrolled in any plan, so the
    dependent load is rejected upstream (documented BLOCKER,
    objects/Benefits/README.md). The report is nonetheless correct and its shape
    is proven live against the same base table and key map — it will return our
    rows once benefits enrollment is configured. See the PR body for the
    standalone paging evidence (the same nine-column query run over the broader
    HRC_SQLLOADER set pages then empties, and the production _BENDEP predicate
    returns zero).

    NINE response columns, in contract order:
      OBJECT_TYPE, RECORD_KEY, SOURCE_TYPE('BASE'), FUSION_STATUS('SUCCESS'),
      FUSION_ID (base PER_BNFTS_BAL_ID), ERROR_MESSAGE (NULL),
      LOAD_REQUEST_ID (NULL), SOURCE_REF (= SourceSystemId), DMT_REFERENCE (NULL).
    SIX parameters: P_RUN_ID, P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID, P_IMPORT_ESS_ID, P_PREFIX,
      P_CHUNK_SIZE, P_AFTER_KEY.
    KEYSET pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY cursor, P_CHUNK_SIZE page).
      LOAD_REQUEST_ID / P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base for an HDL
      load, so BASE-tier matching is by run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID
      is returned NULL per the brief's column mapping.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="ben_depend_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT
    object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
    fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id, source_ref, dmt_reference
FROM (
    -- BASE tier: positive proof in the HCM Benefits base table. The HDL load
    -- writes one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per dependent
    -- (OBJECT_NAME='PersonBenefitBalance', SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER')
    -- whose SURROGATE_ID is the BEN_PER_BNFTS_BAL_F.PER_BNFTS_BAL_ID. Joined to
    -- the base table so FUSION_ID is guaranteed a real base-table primary key.
    -- One row per migrated dependent.
    SELECT 'BenDependent'                 AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id             AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           MAX(b.per_bnfts_bal_id)        AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           m.source_system_id             AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    JOIN   ben_per_bnfts_bal_f b
           ON b.per_bnfts_bal_id = m.surrogate_id
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'PersonBenefitBalance'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE '%\_BENDEP' ESCAPE '\'
    GROUP BY m.source_system_id
)
-- Keyset predicate. An empty P_AFTER_KEY (first page) binds to NULL in BIP, so
-- treat NULL as "from the start": every non-null RECORD_KEY sorts after the
-- empty string. On later pages P_AFTER_KEY carries the previous page's last
-- RECORD_KEY and only greater keys are returned.
WHERE  (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR record_key > :P_AFTER_KEY)
ORDER BY record_key
FETCH FIRST :P_CHUNK_SIZE ROWS ONLY
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="ben_depend_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_REF"      value="SOURCE_REF"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_REF"/>
          <element name="DMT_REFERENCE"   value="DMT_REFERENCE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="DMT_REFERENCE"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <!-- Keyset pagination: page size + cursor. The reconciler calls with an
         empty P_AFTER_KEY first, then passes the last RECORD_KEY received on
         each next call, until a short page returns. -->
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
